 Inventory Management in Ansible

Today I learned how Ansible knows which servers to manage using inventories.

 A well-structured inventory is the foundation of scalable automation.

🔹 Static Inventory
Static inventory is a file that:
Lists managed hosts
Defines IPs or hostnames
Uses INI or YAML format
It’s simple and commonly used for small to medium environments.

🔹 Hosts & Groups

Hosts can be:
Individual servers
Organized into groups

Grouping helps:
Apply tasks to multiple servers
Separate environments like dev, test, prod
This improves readability and control.

🔹 Group Variables
Group variables allow:
Defining variables for a group of hosts
Reusing configuration values
Avoiding duplication
They help maintain consistent configurations.

🔹 Inventory Best Practices
Good practices include:
Meaningful group names
Environment-based grouping
Avoid hardcoding sensitive data
Clean inventories reduce errors.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Inventory defines targets.
 Groups simplify management.
 Best practices ensure scale.
